%U A399674 4083054766617170750038960088,78489326962837656897329703091136,2998593554171963907411447133634132840
%N A399674 Number of reducible flow graphs on n unlabeled nodes with self-loops allowed and distinguished entry r and exit t (r = t if n = 1, else r != t), counted up to isomorphism fixing r and t.
%C A399674 Computed exactly by the equivariant Burnside recurrence (see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program of A397968).
%D A399674 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A399674 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A399674 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A399674 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A399674 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A399674 The same Burnside sum and equivariant entry-exit recurrence as the loopless version, with an additional factor 2^(c(mu)+2) for invariant self-loops at the two fixed endpoints and on the cycles of the remaining permutation; a(1)=2 separately.
%o A399674 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_cfgs_single_sink_loops", 16) # See Python link in A397968 for program code.
%Y A399674 Cf. A397968 (entry-only loopless version), A350794.
%K A399674 nonn,new
